# Integer128 literal below the minimum

Binds -170141183460469231731687303715884105728, whose unsigned part exceeds
the 128-bit range, to verify the literal is rejected with a compile-time
diagnostic, consistent with int8 and int64.

>>> source
too_small: int128 = -170141183460469231731687303715884105728
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `170141183460469231731687303715884105728` for type `int128`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 21, end: 60 }

<<< exit
1
